.TH SDL_ReadU8 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ReadU8 \- Use this function to read a byte from an
.BR SDL_IOStream .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ReadU8(SDL_IOStream *src, Uint8 *value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will return false when the data stream is completely read, and
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
will return
.BR SDL_IO_STATUS_EOF \[char46]
If false is returned and the stream is not at EOF,
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
will return a different error value and
.BR SDL_GetError ()
will offer a human-readable message\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I src
the
.BR SDL_IOStream
to read from\[char46]
.TP
.I value
a pointer filled in with the data read\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure or EOF; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

